::{{Диалог}} I'd like to know more about Tamila...
:::'''Celine:''' You are as curious as a child. But I don't have much to offer.
:::'''Celine:''' Although Tamila's voice is a bit deep, her acting and singing skills are not much of a problem. She's got a lot of fans.
:::'''Celine:''' It's just that... she seems to be unhappy with me, which I'm a little confused about...
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why is she unhappy with you?
::::'''Celine:''' I don't know... Maybe I'm overthinking it but during the rehearsals recently, I felt that Tamila didn't want to lip-sync...
::::'''Celine:''' Also... *sigh* I shouldn't say this but I don't feel comfortable with Tamila's recent public criticism of the lyrics.
::::'''Celine:''' Although the songs she criticized were for her character, I was responsible for the voice-over.
::::'''Celine:''' It just feels like she was aiming that at me... Have I done something to get on her bad side?
::::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Musicals need voice-overs?
:::::'''Celine:''' Usually, no. But the director insisted that I do the voice over for Tamila's songs.
:::::'''Celine:''' He said, "Tamila's voice isn't catchy and girly enough."
:::::'''Celine:''' This is my private affair. Please don't be bothered by it.
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
::::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Then why is she considered the mainstay of the theater?
:::::'''Celine:''' Shhh, don't say that. Tamila's performance skills are top-notch and the audience loves her.
:::::'''Celine:''' It's just that the director said that Tamila's voice isn't catchy and girly enough, so he invited me to do the singing.
:::::'''Celine:''' This is my private affair. Please don't be bothered by it.
::::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why don't you perform on stage yourself?
::::'''Celine:''' I've been thinking about that lately... I want to set foot on a new path.
::::'''Celine:''' I've loved singing since I was a little girl... I could sing all day long, no matter what the song is.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Did anything happen between the two of you?
::::'''Celine:''' I don't think so. We teamed up a few times and it always went well.
::::'''Celine:''' As for outside of the theater... well, Tamila is a star, after all, so I really don't have much contact with her. I don't know what she could be mad about.
::::'''Celine:''' ...maybe I'm just overthinking it. It's probably just because we have different perspectives.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Maybe she is jealous of your voice.
::::'''Celine:''' Shhh. Don't speak so rashly. Tamila's voice is deep but I think it's very touching, especially when she's singing lyrical type songs...
::::'''Celine:''' For example, the contralto in ''Back to the Night'' is something that's beyond me. "I saw the tears in your eyes tonight, will you still love me after dawn~"
::::'''Celine:''' Tamila is a natural beauty and she has a great stage presence. I'm sure she isn't jealous of me... Let's not think too negatively about people.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Выход}} Don't let it bother you too much.
:;(If {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 101150231-->)
:{{Диалог}} How have things been?
:::'''Celine:''' Ah, it's you! Well, I've been taking several roles in different musicals. Just the rehearsal times have me so busy that I can hardly stop to catch my breath!
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you going to be a big star?
::::'''Celine:''' Oh my, don't say that. I'm not going to be some big star. I was the lead actress in a new play, but critics panned it as being too cliché...
::::'''Celine:''' They even said something like, "Belobog has changed, but its musicals are still singing the same ole tune." The point is, after that, I start taking on small roles. I want to polish my acting chops.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Congratulations!
::::'''Celine:''' There's nothing to congratulate me for. I've just been landing several small parts. Even just rushing to venues is no easy feat.
::::'''Celine:''' I had a lead role in a new play, but it didn't get good reviews...
::::'''Celine:''' Some critics said that Belobog has changed, but its musicals are still singing the same old tune. The point is, after that, I start taking on small roles. I want to polish my acting chops.
:;(If {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 101150231-->)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I've got to go. Bye.
:::'''Celine:''' Bye bye. I'll go back to practicing my singing now.
:::'''Celine:''' La la la. "Chasing a mirage, I lose sight of the path in the fog. I only wish for a steady journey through life."

;(Talk to Tamila)
:<!--0.3-second delay-->
:'''Tamila:''' As you can probably tell, my voice is rather low-pitched. The director is not very happy about that, so the theater hired a voice actress to "assist" me.
:'''Tamila:''' She is impeccable indeed... but I too was professionally trained. Never missed a day of practice.
:'''Tamila:''' Now I have to lip sync and act as if in a silent film. I can't help but think that maybe one day they'll get rid of me altogether...
:'''Tamila:''' What do you think I should do?
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Work on your acting.
::'''Tamila:''' *sigh* That won't do. People come to musicals for the songs.
::'''Tamila:''' How embarrassing would it be if a musical performer can't sing with her own voice? It's ridiculous! I'll be like thespians who can't remember their lines and need others to read out the script for them.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why not try acting in a play?
::'''Tamila:''' Both are theatrical arts, true. But the skills they require are hardly transferable.
::'''Tamila:''' Plus, musicals have always been my passion... I don't want to simply give up like this. I still want to give it a go.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Maybe find a project that suits your voice better.
::'''Tamila:''' I'm afraid it's not that easy.
::'''Tamila:''' You might not know this, but musical artists only look good on stage for a very limited period of time.
::'''Tamila:''' Once their physiques change or their voice becomes coarse, they have to bid the stage farewell. They'll call it "spending more time with the family," but everyone knows that's the end of their career.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You'll have to challenge that.
:::'''Tamila:''' Even if the theater agreed with me, the audience would not buy it. They have been quite honest in likes and dislikes.
:::'''Tamila:''' But you do have a point... people should be less judgmental.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} There are other types of musicals you can try.
:::'''Tamila:''' The theater manager is convinced that the audience is only interested in love songs aimed at teens. But it's possible that people's taste has changed and the management failed to grasp it.
:::'''Tamila:''' You know what? I'll see if I can bring some artists together and try some new things. How does that sound?
::;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Need to find a way to get your voice assist fired.
::'''Tamila:''' No, I want to keep my job fair and square. I have no interest in theater politics.
::'''Tamila:''' She is one of us after all. I hope she will see her dream come true on stage one day.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Выход}} I can't think of a better way to help.
::'''Tamila:''' No worries. Thanks for listening to me. I feel much better already. Please keep this conversation a secret.

;(Talk to Amo)
;(First interaction)
::'''Amo:''' ...
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Let's talk about your works...
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What do you write then?
::::'''Amo:''' I wrote some horror novels, the quality of which can be described with the name of the genre according to some critics. Some say those novels should never have been written in the first place. For the disaster fiction I did, same critiques also apply.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What kind of rubbish have you produced?
::::'''Amo:''' I wrote some horror novels, the quality of which can be described with the name of the genre according to some critics. Some say those novels should never have been written in the first place. For the disaster fiction I did, same critiques also apply.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Tell me about your ghostwriting.
:::'''Amo:''' Have you heard of ''Tale of the Winterlands'', the fiction that was recently banned? The publisher was actually quite happy with the quality and wanted the author to make some edits on the original so that they can publish it again.
:::'''Amo:''' But they did not expect the author to simply vanish into thin air! The editors had to contact me instead, asking if I can help with the project.
:::'''Amo:''' "Ha! Tale of the Winterlands is just some cheap folklore compiled together. I can give you one hundred thousand to two hundred thousand words with ease. Piece of carrot cake to me." &mdash; That was my response when I took the job. You know how hard it is to finally get something going. I was just trying to impress them but ended up getting way ahead of myself.
:::'''Amo:''' One of the editors had sent me a copy to let me get the feel of it. It wasn't until I started reading that I realized the book was going to be a classic. I had to admit, I couldn't even remotely reproduce the author's creativity and style.
:::'''Amo:''' The editor has made several attempts to contact me since then, but I managed to avoid her each time because I just couldn't deliver.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How would you rate ''Tale of the Winterlands'' now?
::::'''Amo:''' A Masterpiece of a true genius. Maybe the language still has room for polishing, but the wild passion weaved into the plot is other-worldly. For seven hundred years the people of Belobog have been trapped in the snow, their imagination taken away. This book reignited people's desire to look beyond these snow-covered lands...
::::'''Amo:''' Maybe that's why the Architects insist on banning it... I heard that within a month of the book's publication, the number of people that ventured out into the snow and went missing had gone up exponentially.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What's your plan for the future?
::::'''Amo:''' To avoid the editors for the time being.
::::'''Amo:''' And contemplate on what to do for a living if I'm blocklisted... *sigh*
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Don't put so much pressure on yourself.
:::'''Amo:''' Sorry, I've had a difficult time lately...
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Don't give up just yet. Pull yourself up by your bootstraps.
::::'''Amo:''' Hehe, easier said than done.
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Stop comparing yourself to others. Go with your instincts!
::::'''Amo:''' Hah! I'll become a laughingstock in the history of literature if I do that. "Who's this Amo? How dare he write this rubbish and claim to be writing ''Tale of the Winterlands''?"
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No need to stick to one career path. How about doing something else?
::::'''Amo:''' Haha, I did consider doing that, but... writing is my true passion. My writing may be bad, but I feel happy when holding a pen in my hand...
:::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} That's all for my questions.
;(Subsequent interactions)
::'''Amo:''' I always feel this strange calm when I stare at the trashcan, as if finally returning to where I belong... Ah, the breeze and the smell...
::'''Amo:''' Oh, don't mind me. I was completely lost in that sense of belonging. I remember you, friend. What brings you here?
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} I hear you need help.
::'''Amo:''' Did you? You know, I often come here to contemplate life. When I am looking at that trashcan, I feel like I am looking at myself. I'm close to 30 but I haven't achieved anything in life.
::'''Amo:''' A few days ago, I came here like I always do, and I found a beautiful postcard lying in the trashcan. Surprisingly, it was addressed to me, it was from "Garbage King."
::'''Amo:''' I've heard things about this "Garbage King." They say he's a mysterious scavenger and nobody knows who he really is. Maybe I've been hanging around this trashcan for so long that I caught his attention.
::'''Amo:''' At first, I thought I trespassed somebody's territory and this was a warning... Unexpectedly, the postcard is full of encouragement. He said he's read my novel and he really loves my stories. He told me not to give up. It was really...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Touching...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Suspicious...
::'''Amo:''' No... devastating!
::'''Amo:''' Maybe he's just trying to cheer me up. But from his words, I see a writer much more talented than myself.
::'''Amo:''' Look &mdash; "The birth of a person is like rubbish landing in the trashcan. There's a pleasant sound and it brings joy to people." What a wonderful metaphor. It's like I am reading about wars in the distant past...
::'''Amo:''' And this &mdash; "My friend, we have a long life ahead of us and you still have time to experience your life, until Belobog sends off the last trashcan." How much sorrow does one have to endure before one can write such romantic prose?
::'''Amo:''' Words that take me ages to come up with seem so easy to him. I feel like... I am conversing with a "King" who conquered the wind and snow. Like he is a saint while I am just an insignificant vagrant!
::'''Amo:''' Now I can't focus on anything else. If you know anything about this "Garbage King," please let me know.
::'''Amo:''' I want to know who he is, where he comes from and what he has been through. At least I want to understand the gap between us...
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} This is the clue you are looking for.
::'''Amo:''' Another postcard... Unbelievable. Has he been watching me?
::'''Amo:''' What a weirdo. I still can't believe he's a scavenger... Does he actually have another identity and is he doing this to experience another kind of life?
::'''Amo:''' I can feel it. Inspirations shoot into my head. These are the ideas I've never had... Anyway, thank you. I will cherish these two postcards.
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} I'll help you exercise your rightful rights!
::'''Amo:''' Oh, it's you. Seems like there are still plenty of good people in this world... That's good.
::'''Amo:''' My situation... is this. I'm the ghostwriter of the sequel for ''Tale of the Winterlands'', but I just can't manage to copy the feelings of the original...
::'''Amo:''' That's why an editor is hot on my trail... She recently found out where I live and keeps visiting me, but I don't have any manuscripts to show her!
::'''Amo:''' That editor is named Nika, and my commission to you is to get her away from me &mdash; I don't care how you do it or what you say to her. It'd be best if she thinks Amo is gone and never coming back.
::'''Amo:''' Can you do that? If you can't, then I'll think of something else...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Leave it to me. I'll talk to her.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm very good at persuading people! Leave it to me!
:::'''Amo:''' Now that you've said that, I'm even more concerned...
:::'''Amo:''' Sorry. Maybe I'm being too pessimistic. Don't take it to heart.
::'''Amo:''' Please! You have my sincerest thanks!
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} This is what Nika said.
::{{Black Screen|You told Amo what Nika had said...}}
::'''Amo:''' ...So that's how it is.
::'''Amo:''' This is a trap. I won't fall for it. She just wants to find and torture me, lock me up, and force me to write...
::'''Amo:''' I'm never leaving my trashcan! This is my only home...
::'''Amo:''' Ah... I'm sorry. I was so engrossed in feeling sorry for myself that I forgot to thank you.
::'''Amo:''' Thank you for running the errand for me. These are my only savings. Please take them...
